  "function_code": 163,
  "name": "Analog Segment Buffer",
  "description": "The analog segment buffer function code takes a snapshot of four analog values simultaneously. Simultaneous snapshots eliminate the possibility of inconsistent data within a segment. Any series of segment buffer blocks (analog or digital) unbroken by nonbuffer blocks is an uninterruptible sequence within a segment. Thus, all outputs of the series of blocks are consistent for the duration of the segment cycle.",
  "description_lines": [
